---
Title: unknown lexers
---

A fence in a language minted has no Pygments lexer for prints as plain text in
LaTeX (with a warning), instead of stopping the compile.

```query
tag:#project
```

```tasks
not done
due before tomorrow
```

```kanban
## Todo
- [ ] write
```

```dataview
TABLE file.mtime FROM "notes"
```

```dataviewjs
dv.list(dv.pages().file.name)
```

```base
filters:
  - file.hasTag("x")
```

```mermaid
graph LR
  A --> B
```

A `tabbing` fence is no longer code at all: it is LaTeX's tabbing
(tabbing.js), so it gives no warning.

```tabbing
Name |= Value
width |> 10
```

```ad-note
title: An admonition
Body text.
```

A known language is unchanged, and only the first word of an info string is
the language:

```python title="example.py"
print("hello")
```
